# Running Backend Tests

PHPUnit **must run inside Docker** (PHP 8.3).

## Prerequisites

- Compose file: `../docker/docker-compose.yml` (relative to `backend/`)
- Container service: `backend` (working dir: `/var/www/backend`)
- Tests use SQLite in-memory (`phpunit.xml`) — MySQL does not need to be up for unit tests

## Commands (preferred for agents)

Run from repo paths, with Docker available:

```bash
# Full suite (stack can be stopped — creates a one-off container)
cd ../docker && docker compose run --rm --no-deps backend ./vendor/bin/phpunit tests

# Full suite (faster when stack is already up)
cd ../docker && docker compose exec -T -w /var/www/backend backend ./vendor/bin/phpunit tests

# Single test class or method
cd ../docker && docker compose exec -T -w /var/www/backend backend ./vendor/bin/phpunit --filter 'PublicScammerControllerTest::testScammerSearchByCardNumber'

# Debug output (echo / print_r / var_dump) — use --debug, not --verbose
cd ../docker && docker compose exec -T -w /var/www/backend backend ./vendor/bin/phpunit --debug --filter 'PublicScammerControllerTest'

# Architecture check (PHPArkitect). Run with the suite after PHP or test changes.
cd ../docker && docker compose exec -T -w /var/www/backend backend composer run check:architecture

# Architecture check when the stack is stopped
cd ../docker && docker compose run --rm --no-deps backend composer run check:architecture
```

## VS Code tasks (human workflow)

When the workspace root is `backend/`:

| Task | Use when |
|------|----------|
| `[ALL] Start Services` | Start Docker stack before `exec`-based runs |
| `[Backend] Run PHPUnit Tests` | Run all tests via one-off container |
| `[Backend] Run PHPUnit Tests (debug output)` | Inspect `echo` / `var_dump` output |

## DevSense Test Explorer

Configured in `.vscode/settings.json` via `.vscode/run-phpunit-in-docker.sh`. Requires the `backend` container to be running. Uses `--teamcity` internally — do not add `--verbose` (removed in PHPUnit 12).

## Agent checklist

1. After changing PHP or test code, run the filtered or full suite command above, then `composer run check:architecture`.
2. Report pass/fail from both command outputs; do not assume green without running them.
3. If `exec` fails because the container is down, use `docker compose run --rm --no-deps` instead.
